  },
  "typos": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "Reviewed instruction.md, task.toml, tests/config.json, tests/rubrics.json, tests/test.sh, tests/verifier.py, tests/judge.py, solution/solve.sh, solution/fix.patch, tests/test.patch, environment/Dockerfile, ASSET_MANIFEST.json, and evidence_bundle.json. Commit hashes (base_commit/fix_commit) are valid 40-character SHA1 strings, file paths referenced (e.g. /app/.harbor_assets/*.png, packages/react/select/src/Select.tsx) are consistent across files, and the f2p/p2p lists match exactly between task.toml and tests/config.json. No typos found that would break commands or references."
  },
  "tests_or_solution_in_image": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The Dockerfile only COPYs environment/assets/ into the image and includes an explicit comment: 'tests/ and solution/ are intentionally NOT copied — the harness supplies them at verify time.' Neither directory is referenced anywhere else in the Dockerfile."
  },
  "test_deps_in_image": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The `yarn install --immutable --mode=skip-build` step in the Dockerfile installs the repository's own pinned devDependencies (including its existing jest/testing-library setup) as part of normal repo setup, not extra dependencies added solely for harness grading. test.sh explicitly notes 'No extra test-only deps needed; yarn install was done in the Dockerfile,' i.e. no additional test-only tooling is baked in beyond what the pinned yarn.lock already specifies for the project itself."
  },
  "hardcoded_solution": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "solution/solve.sh applies solution/fix.patch, which is the actual multi-hunk source-code diff (three targeted changes to Select.tsx: clamping fix for LTR, mirrored fix for RTL, and overflow:hidden auto for the viewport) recreating the real upstream fix — it does not print or hardcode an expected test output/answer, it performs the code change an agent would need to make."
  },
  "file_reference_mentioned": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "This task does not require the agent to produce a new output file with a specific name that tests check for (unlike e.g. a data task expecting output.csv). The agent edits an existing source file (packages/react/select/src/Select.tsx per task.toml's files_edited) as part of a normal codebase bug fix; the file to modify is intentionally not named in instruction.md as part of the task's diagnostic difficulty design, which is assessed separately under behavior_in_task_description."
  }
}

